\f1\b\fs34 \cf2 1. What the paper clearly contributes (and should be acknowledged)
\f0\b0\fs28 \
\
This paper makes a 
\f1\b genuine and non-trivial contribution
\f0\b0  to the literature on climate damages and agriculture by doing three things simultaneously:\
\pard\tqr\tx260\tx420\li420\fi-420\partightenfactor0
\cf2 	1.	
\f1\b Embedding agriculture into a full SFC macro-financial framework
\f0\b0 , instead of treating GDP, prices, and finance as exogenous backdrops.\
	2.	
\f1\b Introducing within-country household heterogeneity
\f0\b0  (six income groups) rather than relying on a representative household.\
	3.	
\f1\b Explicitly modelling food inflation as a monetary\'96financial transmission mechanism
\f0\b0 , rather than a relative price adjustment in a real-exchange economy.\
\
This combination is still rare. The paper is correct in claiming that most AgMIP / CGE / PE approaches fail precisely at these points. The contribution is therefore methodological rather than empirical novelty, and that is fine.\
\
However, methodological ambition raises the bar for internal coherence and political interpretation\'97and that is where the paper becomes vulnerable.\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

